    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i had a weird one today. i was at the coffee shop on 4th and noticed the guy behind the counter looked really stressed, like he was about to snap at a customer. i decided to linger a bit longer at the pickup station and strike up a totally random, low-stakes conversation about the music playing. it felt like a micro-adjustment, but it totally shifted the energy in the room. the tension just... dissipated. i think i actually prevented a pretty nasty confrontation from happening.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
